Paera is world of slaves. Monsters roam the land and noone can say no to anyone else that is considered a superior. The Gods have doomed this place because when the inhabitants were given the right to be free chaos ensued.
One fateful day Vaeras was born. He is the only person born with the ability to say no to anyone he wanted, the only one with free will. He was really kind and growing up he
learned that saying no was met with disdain and revenge so he learned to keep his ability a secret.
He's 17 now and in love with Faey, a former classmate. He knows that if he asks her for something sexual she could never say no since he was a better student than her but he wants her to truly love him.
He realizes that no matter what happens he could never learn if she truly loves him unless this world is freed.
He embarks on a journey to find Aema ,the Goddess said to be responsible for this situation Paera is in.
After many adventures he finds her and tries to convince her to free everyone. She tells him that if he can guarantee that this is truly the best course of action
for the people of Peaera she shall comply.
The people welcome him as hero and crown him as king. He tries to find a way to convince Aema that letting people say no to their superiors is benevolent for them.
He gathers the most powerful monsters of the land and drives them to the main city. The monsters are ready to attack and the people get ready for war. As they're about to atack he orders them to stand down.
With him as king noone can say no to him. And as such the monsters start advancing with no resistance. People call him a traitor and a villain but he tells them that love will win in the end.
He then calls upon Aema to watch as the monsters devour the whole city. Aema understands and frees the people who are now allowed to fight back.
Aema thanks him for the love lesson that he taught her and vows to let people have free will going forth.
Vaeras confesses his love to Faey, she responds with a heartfelt yes and theyb both live happily ever after.
